<title>LUXEMBOURG: French strike to hit Luxair flights.</title>
<headline>French strike to hit Luxair flights.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Luxembourg state airline Luxair SA said on Tuesday it had cancelled Thursday's flights to and from Paris, Madrid and Lisbon due to a national French public sector strike which will cut air traffic control cover.</p>
<p>Luxair, partly owned by Germany's Lufthansa, said in a statement it had cancelled the stopover in Strasbourg of its Luxembourg-Vienna flight on Thursday. It scrapped four of its eight flights to and from Paris on Wednesday due to a French firemen strike.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
